{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-f76d30d1-b12e-4498-9ac1-0cb815ebb907","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d29da6aa0084a84","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-a863mpsi/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8004 (Default Vector Store for Gen AI Studio)\n\n## Input Health Warnings\n\n- The strategy body states the full strategy exceeds Jira's size limit and is stored as attachment `RHAISTRAT-8004-strategy.md`. That attachment is not present in the workspace, so the Affected Components table, Impacted Teams table, formal P0/P1/P2 HLR list, Dependencies table, and Non-Functional Requirements could not be parsed. HLRs below are derived from the strategy's Acceptance Criteria and Success Criteria; owner teams are inferred (see Health Warnings).\n- The **Staff Engineer Input** section is non-empty and takes precedence over the (absent) AI-generated technical approach. All staff corrections and directives are logged under \"Staff Engineer Input Overrides\" below and are reflected in the epic scope.\n\n## Staff Engineer Input Overrides\n\nThe following staff corrections and directives override or reshape the AI-generated strategy content:\n\n1. **OGX does not auto-provision PostgreSQL** — OGX defaults to SQLite for application storage; the odh-dashboard gen-ai BFF hardcodes SQLite when creating OGXServer instances. Introducing PostgreSQL is new work, not an extension of existing infrastructure.\n2. **No custom image build, no Konflux onboarding** — `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16` already includes pgvector, and `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` is already in the rhods-operator CSV. The strategy's 1-2 sprint image-onboarding estimate is eliminated; no `repo-onboarding` / `konflux-onboarding` / `license-validation` epics are generated.\n3. **Platform-level shared PostgreSQL via DSC is deferred to RHOAI 3.6** — for 3.5, Gen AI Studio must self-provision its PostgreSQL. The self-provisioning implementation must be designed for portability to the shared connection string in 3.6.\n4. **Hard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164 for operator-based provisioning** — self-provisioning following the model-registry-operator pattern requires a RHOAI-controlled operator, which the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164, In Progress) delivers. Uncertain timing → modeled as a go/no-go Investigation with conditional branches.\n5. **Fallbacks if RHAISTRAT-7164 does not land** — BFF-managed provisioning (like the existing guardrails infrastructure provisioning) or bring-your-own PostgreSQL. The dev team defines a go/no-go gate in sprint planning.\n6. **Auto Rag decoupled** — Auto Rag integration targets RHOAI 3.6 via RHAISTRAT-7824. This strategy validates pgvector only for Gen AI Studio Playground RAG workflows. Auto Rag is removed from affected components, acceptance criteria, and validation (see HLR-3 descoping note).\n7. **Performance thresholds removed** — the default pgvector instance is for development experimentation; no latency SLAs. Sprint 1 benchmark captures the inline Milvus baseline and verifies pgvector is in the same order of magnitude. Flat scan (no index) is sufficient; index-type and corpus-size open questions are removed.\n8. **Resource sizing** — start from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL requests/limits, adjust after benchmarking.\n9. **Vector storage is independent of application storage** — only the vector_io provider (`remote::pgvector` via `ENABLE_PGVECTOR`) is configured; the OGX application storage backend remains SQLite. No SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration concerns; no consolidation of vector and application storage.\n10. **Remote vector store implementation is reusable** — the existing remote vector store implementation in OGX can be largely reused for pgvector; the majority of effort is PostgreSQL/pgvector infrastructure and provisioning.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-E001 | Investigation: default vector store scoping model (per-namespace vs per-instance) | Investigation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 | Investigation: go/no-go on default vector store provisioning approach for RHOAI 3.5 | Investigation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | Enable pgvector remote vector_io provider in the OGX distribution | Implementation | OGX Core | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-E004 | Wire Gen AI Studio playground OGXServer instances to the pgvector vector_io provider | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-E005 | Benchmark pgvector against the inline Milvus baseline and set resource sizing | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E006 | Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector self-provisioning for Gen AI Studio | Implementation (branch A) | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E006 | BFF-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio | Implementation (branch B) | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n\nBranch epics are conditional alternatives selected by the outcome of the provisioning go/no-go investigation; they are attached to that investigation as a plan document, not created as standalone Jira issues.\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 Scoping model investigation\"] --> E004[\"E004 BFF wires OGXServer vector_io\"]\n    E002[\"E002 Provisioning go/no-go investigation\"]\n    E003[\"E003 OGX pgvector vector_io provider\"] --> E004\n    E003 --> E005[\"E005 Benchmark + resource sizing\"]\n    E001 -.-> BR_A[\"BRANCH-A-E006 Operator-based provisioning\"]\n    E001 -.-> BR_B[\"BRANCH-B-E006 BFF-managed provisioning\"]\n    E002 -. selects branch .-> BR_A\n    E002 -. selects branch .-> BR_B\n```\n\nSolid arrows are main-plan blocking edges (dependency → dependent). Dashed arrows are conditional-branch 