xplicit lifecycle and portability caveats).\n- Produce the decision record selecting the approach (or the bring-your-own no-build fallback) and the conditional plan for the selected branch.\n\nOut of scope: implementing either provisioning approach (the selected branch's plan document covers that); deciding the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL via DSC, which is deferred to RHOAI 3.6 by staff direction.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A go/no-go gate is defined and documented (decision date, criteria, owner, escalation path) consistent with sprint planning.\n- [ ] RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery status is assessed against the gate criteria with a recorded conclusion.\n- [ ] A decision record selects exactly one outcome for RHOAI 3.5: operator-based provisioning, BFF-managed provisioning, or bring-your-own PostgreSQL.\n- [ ] The decision record identifies which conditional branch plan applies and any release-commitment implications for this strategy.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (AC-1): A default vector store is available out-of-the-box without manual provisioning. The selected provisioning approach is what makes HLR-1 deliverable in RHOAI 3.5; the branch epics selected by this decision implement it.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The gating question is a human sprint-planning decision dependent on externally controlled delivery timing (RHAISTRAT-7164); the strategy cannot be committed to a specific release until it resolves. This is a schedule risk owned by this investigation, not an acceptance criterion on the implementation epics.\n- The platform-provided shared PostgreSQL via DSC (RHOAI 3.6) is the preferred long-term direction; whatever approach is selected must be portable to consuming a shared connection string later.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":75041,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a525bd1676108484","agent_id":"a771cfebd10ea8693","session_id"