{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9b8e7efe-737b-48ca-bceb-ad621f67180f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8cdada15e9edac85","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-a863mpsi/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E003.md","content":"# Enable pgvector Remote vector_io Provider in the OGX Distribution\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic makes the pgvector remote vector_io provider available and configurable in the OGX distribution so that Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows can use a PostgreSQL/pgvector database running as a separate process instead of the inline Milvus provider. The existing remote vector store implementation in the OGX framework is largely reusable — per the engineering team, the remote pgvector provider already exists in the distribution's provider set — so this epic is configuration and verification work, not new provider development.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Ensure the remote pgvector vector_io provider (`remote::pgvector`, activated via the `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` environment guard) is correctly exposed in the OGX distribution configuration alongside the other remote providers, following the existing provider env-guard pattern used for Milvus and Qdrant.\n- Verify the provider's configuration surface (connection settings, TLS options) accepts the values that a separately provisioned PostgreSQL instance provides, and that it works against the Red Hat `postgresql-16` image (which ships pgvector out of the box — no custom image build and no Konflux onboarding is needed).\n- Confirm the provider runs as a separate process from the OGX server: the vector store is a remote PostgreSQL endpoint, not an inline provider embedded in the OGX process.\n- Verify that OGX's application storage backend is untouched: `storage.kv.type` / `storage.sql.type` remain on their existing SQLite default. This epic changes only the vector_io provider configuration; there is no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL application-storage migration and no consolidation of vector and application storage.\n- Add or extend tests covering the pgvector provider activation and basic vector insert/query behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An OGX server started with the pgvector provider enabled and a reachable PostgreSQL endpoint with pgvector registers the remote pgvector vector_io provider and serves vector insert/query operations through the vector I/O API.\n- [ ] The pgvector provider is activated by configuration only (environment guard), with no code changes required to switch from the inline provider, and the distribution image is unchanged apart from configuration.\n- [ ] The provider operates against a remote PostgreSQL instance running as a separate process; no vector store runs inside the OGX process.\n- [ ] The OGX application storage backend remains on its existing default (SQLite) — no application storage migration occurs.\n- [ ] Automated tests cover pgvector provider activation and basic vector operations, and the distribution's build/test pipeline is green.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-4 (AC-4): The default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack instance (not an inline provider).\n- HLR-2 (AC-2, partial): Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store — this epic provides the provider capability the playground wiring consumes.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- Per the staff engineer, the remote vector store implementation is largely reusable; if reuse uncovers gaps in the pgvector provider, the additional integration work stays within this epic's scope (provider enablement and verification) and does not change the epic structure.\n- No repo-onboarding, konflux-onboarding, or license-validation chain applies: the distribution repo and build pipeline already exist, and the PostgreSQL image with pgvector is an existing Red Hat image already referenced in the rhods-operator CSV.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":76784,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a525bd1676108484","agent_id":"a771cfebd10ea8693","session_id":"d39aef87-060e-46a9-9cc3-49e77e4ae642","uuid":"71d3cff9-a5f1-47b8-955c-dead11e9b1f7","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:12:04.733Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
