{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-3b741910-8920-4268-8745-17407a88be5c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a47546f23107056e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-a863mpsi/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E006.md","content":"# Operator-Based PostgreSQL/pgvector Self-Provisioning for Gen AI Studio\n\n## Description\n\nThis conditional-branch epic implements operator-based self-provisioning of the default PostgreSQL/pgvector instance for Gen AI Studio, following the model-registry-operator pattern: the RHOAI-controlled operator layer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) manages the PostgreSQL lifecycle (Deployment, Service, storage, credentials) for playgrounds with RAG, and Gen AI Studio consumes a connection string rather than managing the database itself. This branch applies if the go/no-go decision finds that RHAISTRAT-7164 lands in time for RHOAI 3.5.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer, reusing the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioned database pattern: create and reconcile the PostgreSQL instance (from the existing Red Hat `postgresql-16` image, which includes pgvector) with the resource requests/limits recommended by the benchmark, per the adopted vector store scoping model.\n- Manage the database lifecycle: creation when a playground with RAG is configured, credential secret management, and cleanup on deletion, using the operator's reconciliation loop.\n- Wire the image reference for disconnected installs by reusing the `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` environment variable already present in the rhods-operator CSV — no custom image build, no Konflux onboarding, and no new RELATED_IMAGE entry unless the existing variable cannot be shared (in which case add one following the existing pattern).\n- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL via DSC arrives (RHOAI 3.6), Gen AI Studio consumes the shared connection string instead of the self-provisioned instance; keep the connection source replaceable.\n- Add operator tests covering provisioning, reconciliation, and cleanup.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A playground with RAG configured in a namespace gets a PostgreSQL/pgvector instance provisioned automatically (no manual user setup), running as a separate process from the OGX server.\n- [ ] The provisioning follows the adopted vector store scoping model and preserves its multi-tenant isolation guarantees.\n- [ ] The PostgreSQL instance uses the existing Red Hat `postgresql-16` image (pgvector included) with resource requests/limits per the benchmark recommendation, and the image reference resolves in disconnected installs via the RELATED_IMAGE mechanism.\n- [ ] Database lifecycle is managed by the operator's reconciliation loop: deletion of the playground configuration cleans up the instance; credential secrets are managed by the operator.\n- [ ] The connection consumed by the playground's OGXServer wiring comes from a single replaceable configuration point, swappable to the RHOAI 3.6 shared platform connection string.\n- [ ] Operator tests cover provisioning, reconciliation, and cleanup, and the build pipeline is green.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (AC-1): A default vector store is available out-of-the-box without users manually provisioning or configuring external infrastructure.\n- HLR-4 (AC-4, partial): The provisioned database runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance.\n- HLR-5 (AC-5, partial): Provisioning follows the adopted multi-tenant scoping model.\n- HLR-6 (AC-6, partial): Sizing per the benchmark recommendation keeps the instance lightweight.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- This branch exists only if the go/no-go decision selects operator-based provisioning (RHAISTRAT-7164 landing in time for RHOAI 3.5). If that outcome does not hold, this epic is removed in favor of the BFF-managed provisioning branch (or, as a final no-build fallback, requiring users to bring their own PostgreSQL by configuring the OGXServer CR spec with their connection details).\n- This work cannot start before the operator layer from RHAISTRAT-7164 is available; until it delivers, there is no RHOAI-controlled operator where this lifecycle management can live. The upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry RHOAI-specific provisioning logic.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":79497,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a525bd1676108484","agent_id":"a771cfebd10ea8693","session_id":"d39aef87-060e-46a9-9cc3-49e77e4ae642","uuid":"0a6c3d37-2ffb-4646-97a2-ad83cb95dab5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:12:39.483Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
