{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af42b601bd919812","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: 'Investigation: go/no-go on default vector store provisioning approach for\n4\t  RHOAI 3.5'\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tdependencies: []\n11\tinvestigation_signals:\n12\t  question_specificity: 1\n13\t  source_accessibility: 0\n14\t  local_runnability: 0\n15\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n16\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n17\timplementation_type: null\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigation: Go/No-Go on Default Vector Store Provisioning Approach for RHOAI 3.5\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's central delivery uncertainty: how the default PostgreSQL/pgvector instance is provisioned for Gen AI Studio in RHOAI 3.5. Operator-based self-provisioning following the model-registry-operator pattern requires a RHOAI-controlled operator, which the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164, In Progress) delivers — a hard dependency with uncertain timing. If RHAISTRAT-7164 does not land in time, the fallback is BFF-managed provisioning (the gen-ai BFF creates the PostgreSQL Deployment, Service, PVC, and Secret when a playground with RAG is configured), with bring-your-own PostgreSQL as the final no-build fallback. The development team is directed to define a go/no-go gate for this decision as part of sprint planning; this investigation produces that gate and the decision.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Define the go/no-go gate: the decision date, the criteria (RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery status and release-train fit for RHOAI 3.5), the decision owner, and the escalation path.\n35\t- Track the RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery status against the gate date and gather the inputs the decision needs (scope landed, operator layer usable for Gen AI Studio provisioning, release-train milestones).\n36\t- Evaluate the two build outcomes against the adopted vector store scoping model: operator-based provisioning (model-registry-operator pattern, reusing the `postgresql-16` image and `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` reference) vs BFF-managed provisioning (guardrails-infrastructure pattern, with explicit lifecycle and portability caveats).\n37\t- Produce the decision record selecting the approach (or the bring-your-own no-build fallback) and the conditional plan for the selected branch.\n38\t\n39\tOut of scope: implementing either provisioning approach (the selected branch's plan document covers that); deciding the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL via DSC, which is deferred to RHOAI 3.6 by staff direction.\n40\t\n41\t## Acceptance Criteria\n42\t\n43\t- [ ] A go/no-go gate is defined and documented (decision date, criteria, owner, escalation path) consistent with sprint planning.\n44\t- [ ] RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery status is assessed against the gate criteria with a recorded conclusion.\n45\t- [ ] A decision record selects exactly one outcome for RHOAI 3.5: operator-based provisioning, BFF-managed provisioning, or bring-your-own PostgreSQL.\n46\t- [ ] The decision record identifies which conditional branch plan applies and any release-commitment implications for this strategy.\n47\t\n48\t## HLR Traceability\n49\t\n50\t- HLR-1 (AC-1): A default vector store is available out-of-the-box without manual provisioning. The selected provisioning approach is what makes HLR-1 deliverable in RHOAI 3.5; the branch epics selected by this decision implement it.\n51\t\n52\t## Risks / Notes\n53\t\n54\t- The gating question is a human sprint-planning decision dependent on externally controlled delivery timing (RHAISTRAT-7164); the strategy cannot be committed to a specific release until it resolves. This is a schedule risk owned by this investigation, not an acceptance criterion on the implementation epics.\n55\t- The platform-provided shared PostgreSQL via DSC (RHOAI 3.6) is the preferred long-term direction; whatever approach is selected must be portable to consuming a shared connection string later.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8764aeab3391d186","agent_id":"a4e9a9654cdcf4b49","session_id":"d39aef87-060e-46a9-9cc3-49e77e4ae642","uuid":"a14c4c4f-7102-4618-943a-655641d8198e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:20:43.362Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af42b601bd919812","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
