{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-927c2ba54a6a3aa0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E007\n3\ttitle: Document the migration path from the default vector store to an external vector\n4\t  database\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tpriority: P2\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E004\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E005\n15\tai_signals:\n16\t  change_specificity: 1\n17\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n18\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n19\t  existing_foundation: 1\n20\t  open_questions: 1\n21\t  external_dependency: 1\n22\t  human_process_gates: 0\n23\t  repo_access: 1\n24\t  architecture_claims: 1\n25\tai_implementability: High\n26\tai_implementability_score: 8\n27\tinvestigation_signals: null\n28\tjira_key: null\n29\tbranch: null\n30\tgated_by: null\n31\tgate_failure_impact: null\n32\t---\n33\t# Document the Migration Path from the Default Vector Store to an External Vector Database\n34\t\n35\t## Description\n36\t\n37\tThis docs-authoring epic produces the user-facing documentation for migrating off the default pgvector-backed vector store: how a user who outgrows the development-experimentation default points their Gen AI Studio playground's OGXServer instance at an external, production-grade vector database via user-provided connection details in the OGXServer CR spec. It resolves the strategy's migration-path open question (aligning with commonly-used vector database providers for easier migration) as a documentation deliverable that follows the implementation. Content authoring and code are different kinds of work with different review criteria, so this deliverable is separated from the BFF wiring implementation.\n38\t\n39\t## Scope\n40\t\n41\t- Write the user-facing migration documentation: when to move off the default pgvector instance (production-scale vector workloads), and how to configure an OGXServer instance with user-provided PostgreSQL/vector database connection details via the CR spec, aligned with commonly-used vector database providers.\n42\t- Document the constraints carried over from the implementation: the default instance is positioned for development experimentation (no latency SLAs), the migration is a configuration change at the single replaceable connection point, and the OGX application storage backend is unaffected.\n43\t- Place the documentation in the existing Gen AI Studio user documentation set, following its structure and style conventions.\n44\t- Technically review the content against the delivered implementation before publication.\n45\t\n46\tOut of scope: any code changes to the BFF or the OGX distribution; the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL via DSC (RHOAI 3.6) consumption story.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- [ ] Published documentation walks a user through pointing an OGXServer instance at an external, production-grade vector database via the CR spec connection details, including credential handling, with no manual re-wiring of the playground.\n51\t- [ ] The documentation states the positioning of the default store (development experimentation) and the trigger for migrating (production-scale vector workloads).\n52\t- [ ] The documentation is technically reviewed against the delivered implementation (the OGXServer CR spec connection surface and the replaceable connection point as built) and the review sign-off is recorded; any discrepancies found in review are fed back and resolved.\n53\t- [ ] The documentation follows the existing Gen AI Studio documentation structure and style, and builds cleanly in the docs pipeline.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- No HLR is directly satisfied by this documentation deliverable. It resolves the strategy's migration-path open question (recording the path from the default store that satisfies HLR-1 to a production-grade external vector database), complementing the out-of-the-box default rather than implementing it.\n58\t\n59\t## Risks / Notes\n60\t\n61\t- This epic must not be started before the implementation it documents is delivered: the BFF wiring implementation (user-provided connection support and the single replaceable connection point), the OGX distribution provider enablement, and the benchmark/sizing positioning all feed the content. It is blocked on all main-plan implementation work per the docs-last rule.\n62\t- If the OGXServer CR spec connection surface changes after RHOAI 3.5 (e.g., the RHOAI 3.6 shared platform database), the migration documentation needs a follow-up update; that future change is out of scope here.\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98fb192425e37357","agent_id":"a7878a1fe5056a3ff","session_id":"d39aef87-060e-46a9-9cc3-49e77e4ae642","uuid":"530d5260-b8e7-4c68-94f7-3f2acd0d4d1f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:26:17.244Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-927c2ba54a6a3aa0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
