{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3bf757d9dbf1a42","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AI Signal Rationale — RHAISTRAT-8004-E001 (Investigation: vector store scoping model)\n2\t\n3\tInvestigation epic — scored with the 5 investigation signals.\n4\t\n5\t| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n6\t|--------|-------|-----------|\n7\t| question_specificity | 1 | Concrete, enumerable question (per-namespace vs per-instance vs both) with a defined deliverable (decision record) and testable criteria (isolation guarantees, provisioning granularity). |\n8\t| source_accessibility | 1 | The OGX vector_io namespace semantics that determine feasibility are readable source: the ogx-distribution repo and its config, plus the architecture context files for ogx-distribution and ogx-k8s-operator. |\n9\t| local_runnability | 1 | OGX is a Python service runnable locally, and PostgreSQL can be backed by an embedded/bundled server, so namespace-isolation behavior can be exercised without a cluster. |\n10\t| cluster_hardware_dependence | 0 | The gating question (which scoping model to adopt) is answerable from source analysis and local runs; only peripheral confirmation of on-cluster multi-tenant behavior might need a live cluster. |\n11\t| human_judgment_required | -1 | The final scoping choice is a design decision with recorded stakeholder preferences (Gen AI Studio lead prefers per-namespace); sign-off from the team is part of the deliverable. |\n12\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-98fb192425e37357","agent_id":"a7878a1fe5056a3ff","session_id":"d39aef87-060e-46a9-9cc3-49e77e4ae642","uuid":"05c2c796-6a9d-451b-b4b9-31d50a59a77a","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:26:24.755Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3bf757d9dbf1a42","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
